    // Domain Rules are NOT:
    // - request validation rules
    // - authorization policies themselves
    //
    // Purpose:
    // - centralize all "can I do X with this model?" logic
    // - avoid duplicating conditions across Actions, Policies, Orchestrators
    //
    // Typical rule methods:
    // - canBeDeleted()
    // - isEditable()
    // - canBeActivated()
    // - canBeConfirmed()
    // - canChangeStatusTo(...)
    //
    // Rules may contain complex conditions and queries,
    // but they MUST remain pure checks:
    // - return booleans or small decision values
    // - do NOT mutate state
    // - do NOT trigger workflows, Actions, Jobs, or side effects
    //
    // Primary usage:
    // - Policies SHOULD call {{ Model }}Rule::… directly (e.g. {{ Model }}Rule::canBeDeleted($model))
    // - Actions/Orchestrators MAY use them to guard state transitions
    //
    // Do not add fetchRuleClass() on the model — import {{ Model }}Rule in the Policy instead.

    public static function canBeDeleted({{ Model }} ${{ modelVariable }}): bool
